/-!
# The general case of Stacks 053R in algebraic form

`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.AffineNoetherianCase` proves the affine form of
Stacks 053R under the extra hypothesis that `B` is Noetherian. This file removes that hypothesis
by carrying out the descent of the last paragraph of the source's proof: the situation `A ⊆ B`
with `B` of finite type over `A` is the base change of a situation `A₀ ⊆ B₀` with `A₀` a finitely
generated `ℤ`-subalgebra of `A`, and there `B₀` *is* Noetherian.

Concretely, write `B = A[X_1, …, X_n]/I`. For a finitely generated `ℤ`-subalgebra `A₀ ⊆ A` let
`B₀ ⊆ B` be the `A₀`-subalgebra generated by the images of the variables, so that
`B₀ = A₀[X]/(I ∩ A₀[X])`. By `MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq` one may choose `A₀`
so that the two fibres of interest are unchanged, `κ ⊗_{A₀} B₀ = κ ⊗_A B` for `κ` the fraction
field of `A` and for `κ(𝔭)` (`MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv`), and so that `A₀` contains a
prescribed element of `A`.

Condition (2) of the source — invertibility of `g` on the generic fibre — descends because it is
the existence of a factorization `g · b = a` with `0 ≠ a ∈ A`: enlarging `A₀` to contain `a` and
`B₀` to contain `g` and `b` reproduces it. Condition (3), the inequality between the two fibre
dimensions, descends by `MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv` together with
`Stacks.Divisors.ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension`, which replaces the residue field of
`A₀` by that of `A`.

The conclusion is then transported back up. The comparison ring map
`κ(𝔭₀) ⊗_{A₀} B₀ → κ(𝔭) ⊗_A B` is flat, so the induced map of spectra lifts generalizations, and
`Set.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_preimage_of_generalizingMap` carries the statement "this
closed set is the union of the irreducible components it contains" along such a map, the closed
set upstairs being the preimage of the one downstairs.

## Main results

* `Set.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_genericPoints`: a closed set is the union of the
  ambient irreducible components it contains as soon as each of its own generic points is a
  generic point of the ambient space.
* `Set.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_preimage_of_generalizingMap`: being the union of the
  ambient irreducible components it contains passes from a closed set to its preimage along a
  continuous map that lifts generalizations.
* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_mul_eq_algebraMap_of_isUnit_fiber_bot`,
  `Stacks.Divisors.isUnit_fiber_bot_of_mul_eq_algebraMap`: condition (2) of the last paragraph of
  the proof of Stacks 053R is the divisibility of a nonzero element of `A` by `g`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension`: for `T` of finite type over `R`
  and `k → K` an extension of `R`-fields, `dim (k ⊗[R] T) = dim (K ⊗[R] T)`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents`: **Stacks 053R in algebraic
  form, with no Noetherian hypothesis.** Under conditions (1), (2) and the inequality half of
  (3), the support of `g` in `Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B)` is the union of the irreducible components of
  that spectrum contained in it.
* `Stacks.Divisors.fiber_zeroLocus_specMap_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents`: the same conclusion
  read inside the scheme-theoretic fibre of `Spec B ⟶ Spec A` over `𝔭`.

## Implementation notes

The hypotheses are those of
`Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_isNoetherianRing`, from which
the main theorem differs only by the absence of `[IsNoetherianRing B]`; the image of `g` in the
fibre ring is written `algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g`, which is `1 ⊗ₜ g` by
`Algebra.TensorProduct.right_algebraMap_apply`. The `B`-algebra structure on the fibre is
`Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra`, a local instance here.

The residue field extensions `κ(⊥) → κ(⊥)` and `κ(𝔭₀) → κ(𝔭)` along `A₀ → A` are
`Ideal.residueFieldAlgebra`, and the towers over `A₀` are supplied by hand rather than by
`Ideal.isScalarTower_residueField`, so that they are towers for the composite algebra structure
`A₀ → A → κ` that the rest of the argument uses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 053R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/053R)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

/-! ### Transport of the conclusion of Stacks 053R along a generalizing map -/

/-- A closed subset is the union of the irreducible components of the ambient space that it
contains, as soon as the generic point of each of its own irreducible components is the generic
point of an irreducible component of the ambient space. -/
public theorem Set.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_genericPoints {Y : Type*}
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [QuasiSober Y] (W : Set Y) (hW : IsClosed W)
    (hgeneric : ∀ y : W, y ∈ genericPoints W → (y : Y) ∈ genericPoints Y) :
    W = ⋃₀ {Z : Set Y | Z ∈ irreducibleComponents Y ∧ Z ⊆ W} := by
  have : QuasiSober W := hW.isClosedEmbedding_subtypeVal.quasiSober
  refine Set.Subset.antisymm (fun y hy => ?_) ?_
  · let Z : irreducibleComponents W :=
      ⟨irreducibleComponent (⟨y, hy⟩ : W), irreducibleComponent_mem_irreducibleComponents _⟩
    let η := genericPoints.ofComponent Z
    refine Set.mem_sUnion_of_mem ?_ ⟨hgeneric η.1 η.2, ?_⟩
    · exact specializes_iff_mem_closure.mp
        (((genericPoints.isGenericPoint_ofComponent Z).specializes
          mem_irreducibleComponent).map continuous_subtype_val)
    · exact hW.closure_subset_iff.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr η.1.2)
  · rintro y ⟨Z, ⟨-, hZW⟩, hyZ⟩
    exact hZW hyZ

/-- **Being the union of the ambient irreducible components it contains passes to preimages along
a map that lifts generalizations.** This is how the conclusion of Stacks 053R is transported from
a descended situation back to the original one: the comparison map of fibres is flat, hence lifts
generalizations, and the closed set upstairs is the preimage of the closed set downstairs. -/
public theorem Set.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_preimage_of_generalizingMap
    {α β : Type*} [TopologicalSpace α] [TopologicalSpace β] [T0Space α] [T0Space β]
    [QuasiSober α] [QuasiSober β] (f : α → β) (hcont : Continuous f)
    (hf : GeneralizingMap f) (W : Set β) (hW : IsClosed W)
    (hcomponents : W = ⋃₀ {Z : Set β | Z ∈ irreducibleComponents β ∧ Z ⊆ W}) :
    f ⁻¹' W = ⋃₀ {Z : Set α | Z ∈ irreducibleComponents α ∧ Z ⊆ f ⁻¹' W} := by
  have hpre := hW.preimage hcont
  have : QuasiSober W := hW.isClosedEmbedding_subtypeVal.quasiSober
  have : QuasiSober (f ⁻¹' W) := hpre.isClosedEmbedding_subtypeVal.quasiSober
  refine Set.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_genericPoints _ hpre fun x hx => ?_
  have himage := AlgebraicGeometry.mem_genericPoints_of_generalizingMap
    (f := W.restrictPreimage f) (hf.restrictPreimage W) hx
  have hambient : f (x : α) ∈ genericPoints β := by
    obtain ⟨Z, ⟨hZ, hZW⟩, hxZ⟩ := (Set.ext_iff.mp hcomponents (f (x : α))).mp x.2
    let η := genericPoints.ofComponent (⟨Z, hZ⟩ : irreducibleComponents β)
    have hηW : (η : β) ∈ W := hZW (genericPoints.isGenericPoint_ofComponent ⟨Z, hZ⟩).mem
    have hηeq : (η : β) = f (x : α) :=
      congrArg Subtype.val
        (TopologicalSpace.forall_specializes_eq_of_mem_genericPoints himage
          (⟨(η : β), hηW⟩ : W) (hW.isClosedEmbedding_subtypeVal.isInducing.specializes_iff.mp
            ((genericPoints.isGenericPoint_ofComponent ⟨Z, hZ⟩).specializes hxZ)))
    exact hηeq ▸ η.2
  refine TopologicalSpace.mem_genericPoints_of_forall_specializes_eq fun z hz => ?_
  have hfz : f z = f (x : α) :=
    TopologicalSpace.forall_specializes_eq_of_mem_genericPoints hambient _ (hz.map hcont)
  have hzmem : z ∈ f ⁻¹' W := by
    rw [Set.mem_preimage, hfz]
    exact x.2
  exact congrArg Subtype.val (TopologicalSpace.forall_specializes_eq_of_mem_genericPoints hx
    (⟨z, hzmem⟩ : f ⁻¹' W)
    (hpre.isClosedEmbedding_subtypeVal.isInducing.specializes_iff.mp hz))

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-- **The conclusion of Stacks 053R passes along a flat ring map.** If the support of `x` in
`Spec R` is the union of the irreducible components of `Spec R` contained in it, then the support
of the image of `x` in `Spec S` is the union of the irreducible components of `Spec S` contained
in it, for any flat `R → S`: the one support is the preimage of the other, and a flat ring map
lifts generalizations. -/
public theorem zeroLocus_singleton_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_flat
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (φ : R →+* S) (hφ : φ.Flat) (x : R)
    (h : (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {x} : Set (PrimeSpectrum R)) =
      ⋃₀ {Z : Set (PrimeSpectrum R) | Z ∈ irreducibleComponents (PrimeSpectrum R) ∧
        Z ⊆ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {x}}) :
    (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {φ x} : Set (PrimeSpectrum S)) =
      ⋃₀ {Z : Set (PrimeSpectrum S) | Z ∈ irreducibleComponents (PrimeSpectrum S) ∧
        Z ⊆ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {φ x}} := by
  have hpre : (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {φ x} : Set (PrimeSpectrum S)) =
      PrimeSpectrum.comap φ ⁻¹' PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {x} := by
    rw [PrimeSpectrum.preimage_comap_zeroLocus, Set.image_singleton]
  rw [hpre]
  exact Set.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_preimage_of_generalizingMap _
    (PrimeSpectrum.continuous_comap _) hφ.generalizingMap_comap _
    (PrimeSpectrum.isClosed_zeroLocus _) h

end Stacks.Divisors

section Fibre

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra
attribute [local instance] Ideal.residueFieldAlgebra

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-! ### Condition (2): invertibility on the generic fibre -/

/-- **Condition (2) of the last paragraph of the proof of Stacks 053R, unwound.** For `A` a
domain, the image of `g ∈ B` in the generic fibre `K ⊗[A] B` is a unit exactly when `g` divides a
nonzero element of `A`. This is the form in which the condition descends to a subring of `A`. -/
public theorem exists_mul_eq_algebraMap_of_isUnit_fiber_bot
    {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [Algebra A B] (g : B)
    (h : IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g)) :
    ∃ a : A, a ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ b : B, g * b = algebraMap A B a := by
  have h' : IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : Ideal A).Fiber B) g) := h
  obtain ⟨den, hden, mul, hmul⟩ :=
    (IsLocalization.algebraMap_isUnit_iff (S := (⊥ : Ideal A).Fiber B)
      (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid B (nonZeroDivisors A))).mp h'
  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := hden
  exact ⟨a, mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_ne_zero.mp ha, mul, hmul.symm⟩

/-- The converse of `Stacks.Divisors.exists_mul_eq_algebraMap_of_isUnit_fiber_bot`: dividing a
nonzero element of the domain `A` makes `g` invertible on the generic fibre. -/
public theorem isUnit_fiber_bot_of_mul_eq_algebraMap
    {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [Algebra A B]
    (g b : B) (a : A) (ha : a ≠ 0) (hab : g * b = algebraMap A B a) :
    IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g) := by
  have hne : algebraMap A (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.ResidueField a ≠ 0 := fun hzero =>
    ha (Ideal.mem_bot.mp (Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_eq_zero.mp hzero))
  refine isUnit_of_mul_isUnit_left (y := algebraMap B _ b) ?_
  rw [← map_mul, hab, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A B
      ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B),
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.ResidueField
      ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B)]
  exact (isUnit_iff_ne_zero.mpr hne).map _

/-! ### Condition (3): the dimension of a fibre under extension of the residue field -/

/-- For `T` of finite type over `R` and `k → K` an extension of `R`-fields, the two base changes
of `T` have the same Krull dimension. This is what makes condition (3) of the last paragraph of
the proof of Stacks 053R descend: the fibre of `B₀` over `κ(𝔭₀)` and the fibre of `B₀` over
`κ(𝔭)` have the same dimension. -/
public theorem ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension
    {R k K T : Type*} [CommRing R] [Field k] [Field K] [CommRing T]
    [Algebra R k] [Algebra R K] [Algebra k K] [IsScalarTower R k K]
    [Algebra R T] [Algebra.FiniteType R T] :
    ringKrullDim (k ⊗[R] T) = ringKrullDim (K ⊗[R] T) :=
  (Algebra.IsPushout.ringKrullDim_eq k K (k ⊗[R] T) (K ⊗[k] (k ⊗[R] T))).trans
    (ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.cancelBaseChange R k K K T).toRingEquiv)

/-! ### The general case -/

/-- The tower `R → κ(Q) → κ(P)` for `P` over `Q`, for the composite structure `R → S → κ(P)`. -/
private theorem isScalarTower_residueField_of_liesOver {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (P : Ideal S) (Q : Ideal R) [P.IsPrime] [Q.IsPrime] [P.LiesOver Q]
    [Algebra R P.ResidueField] [IsScalarTower R S P.ResidueField] :
    IsScalarTower R Q.ResidueField P.ResidueField :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x => by
    change algebraMap R P.ResidueField x =
      Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P (algebraMap R S) (Ideal.over_def _ _)
        (algebraMap R Q.ResidueField x)
    rw [Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap]
    exact IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R S _ x

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B]
  [FaithfulSMul A B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B]

/-- **Stacks 053R in algebraic form, with no Noetherian hypothesis.** Let `A ⊆ B` be a finitely
generated extension of domains, let `g ∈ B`, and let `𝔭` be a prime of `A`. Assume that the image
of `g` in `K ⊗[A] B` is a unit, where `K` is the fraction field of `A` (condition (2) of the
source), and that the fibre over `𝔭` has dimension at most that of the generic fibre (the
inequality half of condition (3)). Then the support of `g` in `Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗[A] B)` is the union
of the irreducible components of that spectrum contained in it.

This is
`Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_isNoetherianRing` with the
hypothesis `[IsNoetherianRing B]` removed, by the descent of the last paragraph of the source's
proof. -/
public theorem zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents
    (g : B) (p : PrimeSpectrum A)
    (h2 : IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g))
    (h3 : ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) ≤
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B)) :
    (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g} :
        Set (PrimeSpectrum (p.asIdeal.Fiber B))) =
      ⋃₀ {Z : Set (PrimeSpectrum (p.asIdeal.Fiber B)) |
        Z ∈ irreducibleComponents (PrimeSpectrum (p.asIdeal.Fiber B)) ∧
        Z ⊆ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g}} := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨a, ha, b, hab⟩ := exists_mul_eq_algebraMap_of_isUnit_fiber_bot g h2
  obtain ⟨n, presentation, hsurjective⟩ :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.iff_quotient_mvPolynomial''.mp (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType A B)
  obtain ⟨gPoly, hgPoly⟩ := hsurjective g
  obtain ⟨bPoly, hbPoly⟩ := hsurjective b
  obtain ⟨A₀, hadjoin, hfg, hrange, hgenericDescent, hfiberDescent⟩ :=
    MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq (RingHom.ker presentation)
      (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.ResidueField p.asIdeal.ResidueField
      {gPoly, bPoly} (Set.toFinite _) (Algebra.adjoin ℤ {a})
      (Subalgebra.fg_def.mpr ⟨{a}, Set.finite_singleton _, rfl⟩)
  have haA₀ : a ∈ A₀ := hadjoin (Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_singleton a))
  have : Algebra.FiniteType ℤ A₀ := (Subalgebra.fg_iff_finiteType A₀).mp hfg
  have hinjA₀ : Function.Injective (algebraMap A₀ A) := Subtype.val_injective
  have : FaithfulSMul A₀ A := (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective _ _).mpr hinjA₀
  let restriction : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A₀ →ₐ[A₀] B :=
    (presentation.restrictScalars A₀).comp (MvPolynomial.mapAlgHom (Algebra.ofId A₀ A))
  have hrestriction (f : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A₀) :
      restriction f = presentation (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A) f) := rfl
  obtain ⟨gPoly₀, hgPoly₀⟩ := hrange gPoly (by simp)
  obtain ⟨bPoly₀, hbPoly₀⟩ := hrange bPoly (by simp)
  let g₀ : restriction.range :=
    ⟨g, gPoly₀, (hrestriction gPoly₀).trans (by rw [hgPoly₀, hgPoly])⟩
  let b₀ : restriction.range :=
    ⟨b, bPoly₀, (hrestriction bPoly₀).trans (by rw [hbPoly₀, hbPoly])⟩
  let a₀ : A₀ := ⟨a, haA₀⟩
  have : Algebra.FiniteType A₀ restriction.range :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.of_surjective restriction.rangeRestrict
      restriction.rangeRestrict_surjective
  have : IsNoetherianRing A₀ := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing ℤ A₀
  have : IsNoetherianRing restriction.range :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing A₀ restriction.range
  have : FaithfulSMul A₀ restriction.range :=
    (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective _ _).mpr fun x y hxy =>
      Subtype.ext (FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective A B (congrArg Subtype.val hxy))
  let p₀ : PrimeSpectrum A₀ := PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap A₀ A) p
  have : p.asIdeal.LiesOver p₀.asIdeal := ⟨rfl⟩
  have : (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.LiesOver (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A₀).asIdeal :=
    ⟨(Ideal.comap_bot_of_injective _ hinjA₀).symm⟩
  have : IsScalarTower A₀ p₀.asIdeal.ResidueField p.asIdeal.ResidueField :=
    isScalarTower_residueField_of_liesOver (R := A₀) (S := A) _ _
  have : IsScalarTower A₀ (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A₀).asIdeal.ResidueField
      (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.ResidueField :=
    isScalarTower_residueField_of_liesOver (R := A₀) (S := A) _ _
  let genericEquiv := MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv presentation hsurjective restriction
    hrestriction hgenericDescent
  let fiberEquiv := MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv presentation hsurjective restriction
    hrestriction hfiberDescent
  have h3₀ : ringKrullDim (p₀.asIdeal.Fiber restriction.range) ≤
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A₀).asIdeal.Fiber restriction.range) := by
    rw [ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension (R := A₀)
        (k := p₀.asIdeal.ResidueField) (K := p.asIdeal.ResidueField),
      ringKrullDim_tensor_eq_of_fieldExtension (R := A₀)
        (k := (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A₀).asIdeal.ResidueField)
        (K := (⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.ResidueField),
      ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv fiberEquiv.toRingEquiv,
      ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv genericEquiv.toRingEquiv]
    exact h3
  have hcomponents₀ := zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_isNoetherianRing
    g₀ p₀ (isUnit_fiber_bot_of_mul_eq_algebraMap g₀ b₀ a₀
      (fun h => ha (congrArg Subtype.val h)) (Subtype.ext hab)) h3₀
  let extension := Algebra.TensorProduct.map
    (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom A₀ p₀.asIdeal.ResidueField p.asIdeal.ResidueField)
    (AlgHom.id A₀ restriction.range)
  have hextension : extension.toRingHom.Flat :=
    RingHom.Flat.tensorProductMap (RingHom.Flat.of_isField (Field.toIsField _) _)
      (RingHom.Flat.of_bijective Function.bijective_id)
  let comparison := fiberEquiv.toRingEquiv.toRingHom.comp extension.toRingHom
  have hcomparison : comparison.Flat :=
    hextension.comp (RingHom.Flat.of_bijective fiberEquiv.bijective)
  have helement : comparison
      (algebraMap restriction.range (p₀.asIdeal.Fiber restriction.range) g₀) =
      algebraMap B (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) g := by
    change fiberEquiv (extension ((1 : p₀.asIdeal.ResidueField) ⊗ₜ[A₀] g₀)) = _
    rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul, map_one, AlgHom.id_apply,
      MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv_tmul]
    rfl
  have hgoal := zeroLocus_singleton_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_flat comparison hcomparison
    (algebraMap restriction.range (p₀.asIdeal.Fiber restriction.range) g₀) hcomponents₀
  rwa [helement] at hgoal

/-- **Stacks 053R, read in the scheme-theoretic fibre of an affine morphism, with no Noetherian
hypothesis.** Under conditions (1), (2) and the inequality half of (3), the support of `g` inside
the fibre of `Spec B ⟶ Spec A` over `𝔭` is the union of the irreducible components of that fibre
contained in it.

This is `Stacks.Divisors.zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents` transported along
`AlgebraicGeometry.fiberSpecHomeo`. -/
public theorem fiber_zeroLocus_specMap_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents
    (g : B) (p : PrimeSpectrum A)
    (h2 : IsUnit (algebraMap B ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B) g))
    (h3 : ringKrullDim (p.asIdeal.Fiber B) ≤
      ringKrullDim ((⊥ : PrimeSpectrum A).asIdeal.Fiber B)) :
    let f := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))
    (f.fiberι p) ⁻¹' (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} : Set (PrimeSpectrum B)) =
      ⋃₀ {Z : Set (f.fiber p) | Z ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber p) ∧
        Z ⊆ (f.fiberι p) ⁻¹' (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus {g} : Set (PrimeSpectrum B))} :=
  (fiberSpecHomeo A B p).symm.eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents_of_image
    (by
      rw [← fiberSpecHomeo_image_preimage_zeroLocus A B p g, Set.image_image]
      simp only [Homeomorph.symm_apply_apply, Set.image_id'])
    (zeroLocus_fiber_eq_sUnion_irreducibleComponents g p h2 h3)

end Stacks.Divisors

end Fibre

end
